3097-Richard Groom, the youngest son of Arthur Groom (co-founder of Binna Burra Lodge and the National Parks Association of Queensland) grew up at Binna Burra. Richard’s book, The View Through the Windscreen, provides a unique insight into the history of Binna Burra and the pioneering men and women who created a Lodge on the edge of Lamington National Park. It is also a story of personal love and loss, of success and failure, of fortune and fire.
